WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.320
- We have witnessed history.

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.280
For the first time ever,

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.890
Congress has criminally
referred a former President

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.150
for criminal prosecution.

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.310
Even Nixon and Andrew
Johnson were never referred

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.650
to the Justice Department
for criminal prosecution.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:11.910
But what does this mean?

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:13.110
What is a criminal referral?

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.850
And what was the January 6th Committee

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.200
basing its findings on?

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.207
Well,

00:00:17.207 --> 00:00:18.270
throughout the January 6th
Committee's hearings this summer

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:19.980
and fall, Committee has presented evidence

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.420
of Donald Trump's attempt
to remain in power

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.150
despite tens of millions of
Americans, more importantly,

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.490
306 real members of the electoral college

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:27.930
which are more important than millions

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:30.120
of Americans saying no.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.800
They've also presented
eyewitness testimony

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.760
and depositions about the way

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.260
that Trump's deranged insistence

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.390
the election had been
stolen resulted in an armed

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.250
and deadly insurrection
on the Capitol building.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.870
The Committee interviewed
Georgia Secretary of State,

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.610
Brad Raffensperger, about
his perfect phone call

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:42.443
with Donald Trump.

00:00:42.443 --> 00:00:44.910
Raffensperger testified that
Trump called him asking him

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:48.060
to find 11,000 ballots
to help flip Georgia

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.080
from its blue reality.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.030
The Committee heard testimony
from a slew of White House

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.010
and other government officials
that they had told Trump

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:56.340
that his election denial stuff
was absolutely not correct.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.720
But that Trump totally ignored

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.220
and disregarded their pleadings.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.320
There was memorable testimony
from 26-year-old aide

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.780
to chief of staff Mark
Meadows, Cassidy Hutchinson,

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.250
who testified that Meadows suggested

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.960
he knew beforehand about the insurrection

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.850
that would happen on January 6th.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.220
- I found Mr. Meadows in
his office on the couch.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.777
I remember leaning against
the doorway and saying,

00:01:13.777 --> 00:01:17.010
"I just had an interesting
conversation with Rudy, Mark.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.620
Sounds like we're going
to go to the Capitol."

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.300
He didn't look up from his phone

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:25.140
and said "Things might get
real, real bad On January 6th."

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.580
- She also testified that Trump wanted

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.170
to give armed protestors entry

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.970
to where he was giving his speech,

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:32.070
so much so that he demanded
all metal detectors

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:34.260
or mags be removed from the area.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.280
- He was angry

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.930
that we weren't letting
people through the mags

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:37.890
with weapons.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.237
I overheard the President say
something as the effect of,

00:01:40.237 --> 00:01:42.870
"Let my people in, they can
march the Capitol from here."

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.120
- Of course, there was
also the ketchup anecdote.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.120
- I left the office and went
down to the dining room.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:52.290
I first noticed there was
ketchup dripping down the wall

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.940
and there was a shattered porcelain plate.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:58.620
The President was extremely angry

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.800
and had thrown his lunch against the wall.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.910
- But in the final public hearing

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:04.680
of the January 6th
Committee, Bennie Thompson

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:05.513
and the other eight members

00:02:05.513 --> 00:02:07.230
of the bipartisan group
laid out, arguably,

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.150
the most damning evidence
of both Trump's apathy

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.340
towards the 2020 Presidential election

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.890
and Trump's thundering
silence for 187 minutes

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.354
while insurrectionists
overran the Capitol.

00:02:16.354 --> 00:02:18.750
Trump's White House
counsel, Pat Cipollone,

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:20.880
and Hope Hicks testified
to Trump's silence

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:21.810
during the insurrection.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:24.480
- [Cheney] So, are you
aware of any phone call

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.490
by the President of the United States

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.070
to the Secretary of Defense that day?

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.570
- Not that I'm aware of, no.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:31.530
- But make no mistake though,

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.810
Trump was definitely busy
strengthening his case

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:36.750
for section 1512 and 1505 obstruction.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.150
- The President was making
phone calls that afternoon,

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.430
but they weren't to law
enforcement officials,

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:43.230
rather President Trump continued

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:45.870
to call his lawyer Rudy Giuliani.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:49.050
Both President Trump
and Mr. Giuliani spoke

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.390
with congressional
leaders to encourage them

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.850
to continue delaying the session.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.890
- Finally, the lawyers in the
Trump White House testified

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.230
about his Nixon-esque plot to
replace the Attorney general

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.490
with a brazen sycophant.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.480
- President Trump tried

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.600
to install a loyalist named Jeffrey Clark

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.240
to lead the department as
Acting Attorney General.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.470
- Now, that's just skimming
the surface for some

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.330
of the evidence that the
January 6th Committee unearthed

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:12.240
and presented in support of
their criminal referrals.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.430
But what is a Congressional
criminal referral?

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.350
Well, a criminal referral
is a recommendation

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:19.380
from a congressional Committee
to the Justice Department

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.360
that, based on certain
evidence, the Committee believes

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.160
that people committed certain crimes.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.720
When Congress makes a criminal referral,

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.160
it has no legal weight.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:27.690
The Department of Justice does not have

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:28.680
to file criminal charges

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.240
just because Congress made a referral.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:33.150
Congress makes law and the
executive branch enforces it.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.800
But that doesn't mean that the referral is

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.810
just Congress handing the DOJ a thick file

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:37.860
and saying "Good luck."

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.680
It is, as we all know by now,
unprecedented for Congress

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.750
to say that a President committed crimes.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.550
The Committee's recommendation
puts more pressure

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:47.010
on the Justice Department and
special prosecutor Jack Smith

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:48.720
to go forward with a prosecution.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.580
And the special prosecutor
statute requires Smith

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.860
to explain the basis for
whatever action he takes,

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.900
including if he declines
to prosecute Trump.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.490
But no doubt the Department
of Justice is going

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:58.530
to be less interested in
the ultimate recommendation

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.420
of Congress and more
interested in the evidence

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.710
that the Committee has gathered.

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.540
So let's talk about the criminal
referrals that were made

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.190
of former President Trump.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:07.530
Representative Raskin said
that the four statutes

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.210
that are named here are not the only laws

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.370
that former President
Trump potentially violated,

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.660
but they are the most important ones.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.610
The first is account of obstruction

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:17.940
of an official proceeding
under 18 USC 1512,

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.773
which makes it illegal

00:04:18.773 --> 00:04:20.760
to corruptly obstruct
an official proceeding.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.920
The Committee report concluded
that Congress' Joint Session

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:23.820
to count electoral votes

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.800
on January 6th was an official proceeding

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.160
under Section 1512, and the
report relies on the decisions

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.150
of the many federal judges

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.560
who have already reached this conclusion

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.660
in cases involving the
January 6th defendants.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.310
As for whether Trump had
the requisite intent,

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:36.457
the Committee concluded that, quote,

00:04:36.457 --> 00:04:38.010
"There should be no doubt
that President Trump knew

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:39.703
that his actions were likely to, quote,

00:04:39.703 --> 00:04:42.000
'obstruct, influence or
impede that proceeding.'"

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.560
And based on the evidence developed,

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.240
President Trump was attempting to prevent

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.740
or delay the counting

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:49.140
of lawful certified
electoral college votes

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.070
from multiple states.

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:52.680
Quote, "President Trump was
directly and personally involved

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.513
in this effort,

00:04:53.513 --> 00:04:55.950
personally pressuring Vice
President Pence relentlessly

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:58.830
as the Joint Session on
January 6th approached."

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:01.230
Quote, "Indeed, in an email
exchange during the violence

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.180
of January 6th, John Eastman admitted

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:05.220
that President Trump had been advised

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.620
that Vice President Pence
could not lawfully refuse

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.260
to count votes under
the Electoral Count Act,

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:12.330
but once he gets something in his head,

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.280
it's hard to get him to change course.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.160
In addition, President Trump
knew that he had lost dozens

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.510
of state and federal lawsuits

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.640
and that the Justice
Department, his campaign,

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.470
and his other advisors concluded

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:24.660
that there was insufficient
fraud to alter the outcome.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.430
President Trump also knew that no majority

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.020
of any State legislature had taken

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.960
or manifested any intention
to take any official action

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:33.330
that could change a State's
electoral college votes."

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.620
And the effort to pressure Mike Pence is

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:37.470
just one possible
violation of 18 USC 1512.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.510
The Committee said that
there is also evidence

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:41.820
to support charges, quote,
"Based on the plan to create

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.170
and transmit to the executive

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:46.140
and legislative branches
fraudulent electoral slates,

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:47.280
which were ultimately intended

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.340
to facilitate an unlawful
action by Vice President Pence

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:53.490
to refuse to count legitimate
certified electoral votes

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.950
during Congress's official
January 6th proceeding."

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.780
In addition to the fake electoral slates,

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:58.680
the Committee found evidence

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:00.480
that Trump may have illegally pressured

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:02.520
state election officials,
state legislators,

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:06.030
and others to, quote, "Alter
official electoral outcomes."

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:07.980
And finally, the report
also says that Trump tried

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:10.290
to corrupt the Department of
Justice, citing his commitment

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:13.027
to the DOJ that all it
needed to do was, quote,

00:06:13.027 --> 00:06:15.823
"Just say that the election was corrupt,

00:06:15.823 --> 00:06:19.320
plus leave the rest to me and
the Republican congressmen."

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:20.670
The Committee also uncovered evidence

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.230
that Jeffrey Clark was
instrumental in trying

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:23.850
to corrupt the Department of Justice

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:25.080
and further into the scheme to interfere

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:26.790
with the official proceeding of Congress

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:27.840
to certify the vote.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:30.990
- Jeffrey Clark was an
Assistant Attorney General,

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.170
a Trump appointee at the
Department of Justice.

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:37.860
According to multiple
sources, Mr. Clark was asked

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:40.470
by then President Trump
to take over the role

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:44.580
of Attorney General in part
so he could issue a series

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:47.940
of letters falsely suggesting
that the Department

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:51.120
of Justice believed the
Presidential election

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.443
may have been stolen.

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:55.260
Of course, this happened

00:06:55.260 --> 00:07:00.000
after the department had
repeatedly informed President Trump

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.810
that his allegations of a
stolen election were not true

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:06.690
and were not supported by the evidence.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:10.140
And this happened after
dozens of courts had ruled

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:13.320
against President Trump and
his election fraud claims.

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:15.877
- Clark sent the letter that
Cipollone described as, quote,

00:07:15.877 --> 00:07:19.267
"A murder suicide pact" in
the hope that it would, quote,

00:07:19.267 --> 00:07:21.210
"Help persuade a state legislature

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:23.100
to change its certified slate

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.900
of electoral college electors based

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:26.550
on false allegations of fraud."

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:28.170
Which was then supposed to inspire Pence

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:30.390
to count a different slate on January 6th.

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:31.260
And according to the Committee,

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:34.020
the letter was transparently
false, improper and illegal.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.850
And in terms of the actual Capitol rights,

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.010
the Committee says that
Trump's action and inaction

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:40.080
during the January 6th
riot was more evidence

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:41.880
of intent to obstruct Congress.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.190
He spent 187 minutes
refusing to take any step

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:45.420
to stop the violence.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:48.630
And instead, Trump and Rudy
Giuliani called members

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:51.240
of Congress who were
sheltering in place to hide

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.100
from the attackers and
asked them to go along

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:55.170
with the illegal Eastman
plan and impede the vote.

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:56.220
And the Committee said that John Eastman

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.830
and Kenneth Chesebro were
instrumental in the conspiracy

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.449
and that representative Scott Perry

00:08:00.449 --> 00:08:02.910
and other republicans who
have resisted testifying

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:05.100
likely have material facts
regarding Trump's plan

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.300
to overturn the election.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:07.920
The second count of the
criminal referral deals

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:10.170
with conspiracy to
defraud the United States.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:13.050
Section 371 of Title 18
makes it illegal to enter

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.420
into a criminal conspiracy
to defraud the United States.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:16.260
The Supreme Court has held

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.580
that the statute criminalizes the use

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:20.040
of deceptive practices in
connection with any conspiracy

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:22.110
for the purpose of impairing, obstructing,

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:24.390
or defeating the lawful
function of any department

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:25.223
of government.

00:08:25.223 --> 00:08:27.180
And conspiring to obstruct
a Joint Session of Congress

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:29.400
from certifying the
election certainly qualifies

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.070
as seeking to obstruct a lawful
function of the government.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:33.630
And the Committee generally
alleges that Trump

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:36.180
and his co-conspirators
followed a seven point plan.

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:38.070
First, engage in a concerted effort

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:39.960
to spread false information
to the American public

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:41.430
that the 2020 election was stolen.

00:08:41.430 --> 00:08:43.140
Second, to orchestrate a corrupt scheme

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:45.090
between Trump Chief of Staff Mark Meadows

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:46.710
and representative Scott Perry

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.210
to replace the acting Attorney General

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:50.310
who rejected Trump's fraud claims.

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:52.710
With Trump's DOJ ally Jeffrey Clark

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.530
to use the Department of Justice
to overturn the election.

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:57.270
Third, to implement Eastman's plan

00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.880
to pressure Vice President
Pence to refuse to count

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:02.010
or delay the certification
of the electoral count.

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:03.930
Fourth, to pressure
state election officials

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.540
and state legislators to
change election results.

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:07.890
Fifth, to instruct Republicans

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:09.330
to create false electoral slates

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:12.450
in seven battleground states
and transmit those fake slates

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:14.370
to Congress and the National Archives.

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:16.530
Six, to summon up a mob in the US Capitol.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:18.990
And seven, during the attack
on the Capitol to ignore pleas

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:20.940
for help and tacitly endorse the violence,

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:23.130
including threats to hang Mike Pence.

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:25.020
As for proof that
individuals use deceitful

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:26.430
or dishonest means, the Committee says

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:27.750
that there were two areas where Trump

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:28.860
and his friends were deceitful.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:31.470
Starting with their insistence
the election was fraudulent

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.090
and that Trump defeated Joe Biden.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.620
There's actually an
incredibly damning chart

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:37.260
on page 17 of the
Committee's report outlining

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.550
what the lawyers were saying

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:39.750
that there wasn't election fraud

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:41.340
versus what Trump was saying

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:43.140
that there was mass election fraud.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:43.973
For example,

00:09:43.973 --> 00:09:45.990
Trump showed then Deputy
Attorney General Jeffrey Rosen,

00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:47.910
a videotape that supposedly
showed a suitcase full

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:48.743
of ballots.

00:09:48.743 --> 00:09:50.707
Rosen explained to Trump that
this was actually, quote,

00:09:50.707 --> 00:09:51.540
"A bin.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:53.490
That's what they use when
their counting ballots.

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:54.323
It's benign."

00:09:54.323 --> 00:09:56.610
One week later, Trump
repeated the conspiracy claim.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:58.770
Quote, "There is even the
security camera footage

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:01.380
from Georgia that shows
officials telling poll watchers

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:04.140
to leave the room before
pulling suitcases of ballots out

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:06.780
from under the tables and
continuing to count for hours."

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:07.950
Attorney General Bill Barr

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:11.130
and Deputy AG Richard Donoghue
debunked Trump's Michigan

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:12.930
and Pennsylvania voter fraud claims.

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:15.150
But once again, Trump
ignored what they were saying

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:16.770
and made up his own facts.

00:10:16.770 --> 00:10:17.970
Trump followed the same pattern

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.140
with other conspiracy theories

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.490
about Dominion voting machines.

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:22.440
And as to motive, the Committee
says that, first of all,

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:24.037
it helped Trump raise money and, quote,

00:10:24.037 --> 00:10:25.830
"Evidence gathered by
the Committee indicates

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:27.600
that President Trump
raised roughly one quarter

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.550
of a billion dollars
in fundraising efforts

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:31.650
between the election and January 6th.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:34.080
These solicitations persistently
claimed and referred

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:36.330
to the election fraud that did not exist."

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:38.550
And the second reason Trump
lied about election fraud was

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:41.010
to obstruct the January 6th
certification proceedings.

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:43.470
Quote, "Trump disregarded
the rulings of the courts

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:45.210
and rejected the findings and conclusions

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:48.480
and advice from his Justice
Department, his campaign experts

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.730
and his White House and Cabinet advisors.

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:52.890
He chose instead to try
to overturn the election

00:10:52.890 --> 00:10:55.703
on January 6th and took a
series of very specific steps

00:10:55.703 --> 00:10:57.630
to attempt to achieve that result."

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:00.210
And this is all related to the
third element of a conspiracy

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:02.340
that the person takes
at least one overt act

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:04.650
in furtherance of the conspiracy.

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:06.570
For Trump to achieve the desired result,

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:07.500
he had to get Mike Pence

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:09.210
to ignore the constitutional duties.

00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:10.043
You might recall

00:11:10.043 --> 00:11:11.340
that the 12th Amendment
gives the Vice President,

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:13.860
in their role as the President
of the Senate, the job

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:16.110
of certifying the results of
the Presidential election.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.810
Quote, "The president of the
Senate shall, in the presence

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:20.520
of the Senate and the
House of Representatives,

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:22.350
open all of the certificates

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:24.060
and the votes shall then be counted.

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:25.890
The person having the
greatest number of votes

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:28.080
for President shall be the President."

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:30.900
The Electoral Count Act of 1887 reiterates

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:32.910
that the Vice President's
role is ministerial,

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:34.860
in that his job is just
to count the votes,

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:38.010
not to choose which votes to
count and which to reject.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:40.380
But while Trump was being told
that he lost the election,

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:42.157
lawyer John Eastman and others, quote,

00:11:42.157 --> 00:11:44.970
"Devised a plan whereby
Vice President Pence would,

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:47.790
as a presiding officer, declare
that certain electoral votes

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:49.680
from certain states could not be counted

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:50.760
at the Joint Session."

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:52.590
John Eastman knew before
proposing this plan

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:53.700
that it was was not legal.

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.560
Despite knowing that the plan was illegal,

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.150
Trump pursued it anyway including

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:00.210
for the 187 minutes when
the attack happened.

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:03.030
Congress was being evacuated
to underground tunnels

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:04.350
and even after he was aware

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:07.080
that the mob was chanting
about hanging Mike Pence.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.760
Count three of the
criminal referral refers

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:12.510
to a conspiracy to make false
statements under 18 USC 1001.

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:15.810
This is the classic lying
to the government provision.

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:17.850
And this count was about Trump
conspiring with other people

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:19.917
to submit slates of fake
electors to Congress

00:12:19.917 --> 00:12:21.150
and the National Archives.

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:22.560
These certificates were patently false

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:24.600
since Biden won each of those states

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:26.880
and the state's authorities
certified Biden's victory.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:29.250
Now, in fairness, whether a
statement or act is material

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:32.970
for the purposes of Section
1001 can be a contentious issue,

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:35.317
but here the report says
that at best, quote,

00:12:35.317 --> 00:12:37.650
"It can hardly be disputed
that the false slates

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:40.740
of electors were material as
nothing can be more material

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:43.650
to the Joint Session of
Congress to certify the election

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:46.890
than the question of which
candidate won which states.

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:48.780
Indeed, evidence obtained
by the Committee suggests

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:51.090
that those attempting to submit certain

00:12:51.090 --> 00:12:53.640
of the electoral votes
regarded the need to provide

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:56.580
that material to Vice
President Pence as urgent."

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:57.413
The bigger question is

00:12:57.413 --> 00:12:59.190
whether the various people
making the certificates

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:01.620
and submitting them acted
knowingly and willfully.

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:03.420
Some of those individuals
who signed their names

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:05.070
to fake certificates
said that they thought

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:07.590
that they'd only be used if
Trump prevailed in litigating

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:09.750
in their states, paving
the way for Trump's win

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:11.400
in those states to be certified,

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:13.230
making their fake certificates valid

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:16.740
and okay to submit to the
National Archives and to Congress.

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:18.930
But that's not the case with most

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:20.160
of the executive branch here.

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:22.320
Since Trump acting through
his co-conspirators,

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:25.350
like Eastman and Chesebro,
relied on the existence

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:27.660
of those fake electors
as a basis for asserting

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.850
that the Vice President could reject

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:32.760
or delay the certification
of the Biden electors.

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:34.170
The people who believed
that they were serving

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:35.940
as alternate electors
in case Trump prevailed

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:37.590
in court might not have known that Trump

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:39.090
and Eastman were
collecting the certificates

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:41.550
for another reason, to persuade Pence

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:42.900
to implement their illegal plan.

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:44.310
But the Committee alleges
that the higher ups,

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:46.650
including Donald Trump,
knew what they were doing

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:49.620
and personally participated in this plan.

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:50.520
Quote, "The evidence is clear

00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:52.230
that President Trump
personally participated

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:55.020
in a scheme to have the Trump
electors meet, cast votes,

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:57.690
and send their votes to the
Joint Session of Congress

00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:00.210
in several states that
Vice President Biden won,

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:02.340
and then his supporters
relied on the existence

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:04.410
of these fake electors
as part of their effort

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:05.910
to obstruct the Joint Session."

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:08.460
And to prove an overt acting
furtherance of a conspiracy,

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:10.440
the Committee relies on the testimony

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:13.230
of Republican National Committee
chairwoman Ronna McDaniel.

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:14.730
She told the Committee that Trump

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:16.260
and Eastman directly requested

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:17.970
that the RNC organized the effort

00:14:17.970 --> 00:14:20.910
to have the fake electors
meet and cast their votes,

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:22.890
and that she complied with their request.

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:24.810
And then the fourth count
of the criminal referral is

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:27.510
for inciting, assisting,
or aiding an insurrection

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:30.750
in violation of 18 USC 2383.

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:32.820
Until the events of January 6th, 2021,

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:35.790
there had been no prosecutions
under Section 2383

00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:37.050
since the Civil War.

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:39.360
The insurrection statute
was enacted in 1862

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:41.790
as a precursor to the
Emancipation Proclamation.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:44.010
And there was an 1863
circuit court case that held

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:45.240
that the act was unconstitutional

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:47.310
because it punished the
same conduct as treason.

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:48.750
And treason was only applicable

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:51.570
if a foreign country levied
war against the United States.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:54.120
Since 1863, the Supreme Court has implied

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:56.790
but has not yet ruled that it
would reject the insurrection

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.887
as an end run around treason argument.

00:14:58.887 --> 00:15:01.530
President Trump was
acquitted of incitement

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:03.750
to insurrection in his
second impeachment trial,

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.460
but since this was not a judicial trial,

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:07.080
there's no double jeopardy problem.

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:08.250
However, it's not easy

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:09.870
to get a conviction under the statute

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:11.700
because it implicates the First Amendment.

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:14.070
The Committee relied on a
recent court opinion to assert

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:16.920
that Trump's speech wasn't
protected by the First Amendment.

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:19.260
In Thompson versus Trump, a
judge on the DC Circuit ruled

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:20.640
that the statements Trump made

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:23.767
during his Ellipse speech
before the riot, quote,

00:15:23.767 --> 00:15:26.760
"Were plausibly words of
incitement not protected

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:27.870
by the First Amendment."

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:29.790
This was a civil case where 11 members

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:31.080
of the US House of Representatives

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:34.470
and two Capitol police officers
sued Trump seeking damages

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:36.150
for physical injuries
and emotional distress

00:15:36.150 --> 00:15:37.350
from January 6th.

00:15:37.350 --> 00:15:39.810
The court ruled that Trump
would not necessarily be able

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:42.330
to invoke presidential immunity
in defending the claim.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:43.230
But you can imagine something

00:15:43.230 --> 00:15:45.060
that is arguably political speech is going

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:47.580
to receive the highest amount
of First Amendment protection.

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:49.200
So we'll see how this one goes.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:50.820
The Committee argues that
it doesn't need to prove

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:52.650
that Donald Trump was actually in contact

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:55.590
with the actual rioters
or that there was evidence

00:15:55.590 --> 00:15:57.420
of an actual agreement
between the President

00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:58.253
and the rioters.

00:15:58.253 --> 00:16:00.840
Quote, "The President need
only have incited, assisted,

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:02.850
or aided and comforted those engaged

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.160
in violence or other lawless activity

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:07.470
in an effort to prevent
the peaceful transition

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:09.330
of the Presidency under our Constitution."

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:10.590
But as an interesting coda here,

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:12.270
although the Congressional
criminal referrals

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:14.040
carry no legal weight, Jack Smith,

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:15.960
who Attorney General
Merrick Garland appointed

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:18.270
as special counsel in charge
of looking into these crimes,

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:20.880
at least as it regards
Donald Trump and others

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:22.620
in that orbit, sent a letter

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:25.432
to the select Committee requesting
all the panel's materials

00:16:25.432 --> 00:16:27.960
from the 18 month probe.

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:30.030
So the special prosecutor is
looking into the evidence,

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:31.950
if not the referrals themselves.

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:34.020
But if the DOJ picks up
the criminal referrals,

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:35.280
whether they convict on any

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:36.600
of these counts will largely depend

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:38.520
